WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
The starting state has manual
API requests and spreadsheets,

00:00:03.474 --> 00:00:06.560
shared environments, and no
virtualized provider backend.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.280
QA engineers collect
and reconcile evidence.

00:00:09.394 --> 00:00:12.960
Vendor test-slot availability
constrains parallel execution.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.400
The modernized state introduces
reviewed REST Assured and JUnit tests,

00:00:18.444 --> 00:00:23.200
delivery-pipeline execution, isolated
fixtures and a validated WireMock provider

00:00:23.253 --> 00:00:28.160
model. Testcontainers supports
repeatable service-test resources.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.320
Raw assertions, traces and run
identifiers survive cleanup.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.960
This foundation creates repeatability
without depending on AI.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:40.080
The AI-assisted state adds
approved context, candidate

00:00:40.136 --> 00:00:44.240
artifacts and evidence-based assistance
around that same execution path.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:50.240
AI drafts tests and fixtures, proposes
relevant scope and diagnoses failures.

00:00:50.366 --> 00:00:55.040
Reviewers approve changes before
existing runners execute them.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:58.640
Compare equivalent payment packs
to distinguish modernization

00:00:58.693 --> 00:01:02.400
gains from incremental AI
benefit. Include review,

00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:06.081
correction, platform overhead
and real-provider checks.

00:01:06.293 --> 00:01:08.800
No measured improvement is
claimed in this scenario.
